ENTRY            G4124   20261007   20261124   20261124       G061
SUBENT        G4124001   20261007   20261124   20261124       G061
BIB                 12         50
TITLE      Mass distribution of the 237Np photofission fragments
           at energy 12.5 MeV
AUTHOR     (O.O.Parlag,V.T.Maslyuk,A.I.Lengyel,Yu.V.Kibkalo)
INSTITUTE  (4UKRIEP,4UKRIJD)
REFERENCE  (J,YFE,10,288,2009)
           #doi:10.15407/jnpae2009.03.288
FACILITY   (MICRT,4UKRIEP)
INC-SOURCE (BRST)
DETECTOR   (GELI) Volume 100cm3.
SAMPLE     Six disks of oxide Np237 with diameter of active layer
            11.5 mm and thickness 20 micron on Ni backing with
            diameter of 30 mm.
           Impurities Pu-238 and Pu-239 in target made 2e-9 and
            6e-7 g accordingly.
           The mass of 237Np on the disks was in the range of
           963 - 1193 mu-g
METHOD     (ACTIV) Induced beta-delayed gamma-activity measured.
DECAY-DATA ((1.)36-KR-85-M,4.480HR,DG,151.195,0.75)
           ((2.)36-KR-87,76.3MIN,DG,402.587,0.50)
           ((3.)36-KR-88,2.84HR,DG,196.301,0.260)
           ((4.)38-SR-91,9.48HR,DG,1024.3,0.335)
           ((5.)38-SR-92,2.71HR,DG,1383.93,0.90)
           ((6.)40-ZR-97,16.744HR,DG,743.36,0.9306)
           ((7.)42-MO-99,66.7HR,DG,739.4,0.1213)
           ((8.)44-RU-103,39.35D,DG,497.1,0.91)
           ((9.)44-RU-105,4.44HR,DG,724.30,0.473)
           ((10.)51-SB-129-G,4.40HR,DG,812.8,0.430)
           ((11.)53-I-131,192.6HR,DG,354.5,1.00)
           ((12.)52-TE-132,78.2HR,DG,228.16,0.88)
           ((13.)53-I-133-G,20.8HR,DG,529.872,0.87)
           ((14.)53-I-134-G,52.5MIN,DG,884.090,0.651)
           ((15.)53-I-135,6.57HR,DG,1260.41,0.287)
           ((16.)55-CS-138-G,33.41MIN,DG,1435.86,0.763)
           ((17.)56-BA-139,83.06MIN,DG,165.86,0.2376)
           ((18.)56-BA-140,12.81D,DG,537.3,0.240)
           ((19.)58-CE-141,32.38D,DG,145.45,0.493)
           ((20.)57-LA-142,91.1MIN,DG,641.3,0.474)
           ((21.)58-CE-143,33.00HR,DG,293.3,0.420)
           ((22.)60-ND-149,1.728HR,DG,114.3,0.192)
ERR-ANALYS (DATA-ERR) The total error in determining the
           cumulative fission fragment yields was estimated
           taking into account the statistical errors in the
           intensity of the total absorption peaks, the analysis
           of time dependences, the spread of the values
           averaged over individual experiments, the errors in
           the interpolated efficiency values and the
           nuclear-physical constants of the fragments (gamma-
           line intensities, half-life periods) was 7-12%.
HISTORY    (20261007C) UkrNDC
           (20261007R) Data received from O.O.Parlag
ENDBIB              50
COMMON               1          3
EN-MAX
MEV
 12.5
ENDCOMMON            3
